  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State vs Kanhaiya Lal (2025:Rj-Jd:43645) on 3 October, 2025 Author: Dinesh Mehta Bench: Dinesh Mehta [2025:Rj-Jd:43645] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Appeal No. 615/1996 State of Rajasthan ----Appellant Versus Kanhaiya Lal S/o Shri Ladu Ram Jat, R/o Moonpura, Tehsil Mandalgarh, District Bhilwara. ----Respondent For Appellant(s) : Mr. Shravan Singh Rathore, Pp For Respondent(s) : Mr. Paramveer Singh Justice Dinesh Mehta Order 03/10/2025 1. The instant appeal has been filed under Section 378(iii) and (i) of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 by the State of Rajasthan against the judgment and order dated 14.06.1996 passed by the learned Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Mandalgarh, District Bhilwara (hereinafter referred to as the 'trial Court') in Criminal Case No.56/87, whereby the trial Court had acquitted the accused-respondent for the charge of offence under section 7/16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration (Pfa) Act of 1954 (hereinafter referred to as the 'Act of 1954'). 2. The State of Rajasthan had filed a complaint against the accused-respondent under the provisions of the Act of 1954 inter alia alleging that the milk which the accused-respondent was selling, was adulterated/contaminated. (Uploaded on 03/10/2025 at 04:32:44 Pm) [2025 : Rj-Jd:43645] (2 of 2) [Crla-615/1996]",
